WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.629
Good morning! Who are you?

2
00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:16.375
I'm a zebra.

3
00:00:16.376 --> 00:00:20.846
We're a lot like horses!

4
00:00:20.847 --> 00:00:23.638
Where do you live?

5
00:00:23.639 --> 00:00:28.633
We live in Africa.

6
00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:34.424
We like grasslands and woodlands.

7
00:00:34.425 --> 00:00:40.731
I like your black and white stripes!

8
00:00:40.732 --> 00:00:44.362
All zebras have stripes.

9
00:00:44.363 --> 00:00:50.109
But every zebra’s stripes look different.

10
00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:52.874
What do you eat?

11
00:00:52.875 --> 00:00:56.426
We graze.

12
00:00:56.427 --> 00:01:01.096
That means we eat a lot of grass.

13
00:01:01.097 --> 00:01:06.481
We move often to find water and food.

14
00:01:06.482 --> 00:01:14.162
You have a lot of teeth!

15
00:01:14.163 --> 00:01:20.057
Our teeth help us bite and chew grass.

16
00:01:20.058 --> 00:01:24.338
They never stop growing.

17
00:01:24.339 --> 00:01:27.702
Do you live alone?

18
00:01:27.703 --> 00:01:33.183
No. We stay with our families.

19
00:01:33.184 --> 00:01:38.212
Our families travel in big herds.

20
00:01:38.213 --> 00:01:42.587
Some herds have thousands of zebras!

21
00:01:42.588 --> 00:01:46.332
Why do zebras bite each other?

22
00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:51.712
Zebras don't really bite each other.

23
00:01:51.713 --> 00:01:55.939
We just use our teeth for grooming.

24
00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:01.050
We keep other zebras' coats clean.

25
00:02:01.051 --> 00:02:04.869
I’m thirsty.

26
00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:09.897
It’s time to look for water again.

27
00:02:09.898 --> 00:02:18.150
Good-bye, Zebra!

